# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private key material. NEVER commit any of this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The licence-signing key is the single most sensitive artefact in the
# commercial layer: anyone holding it can mint licences. It exists only on the
# issuance host and in a secret manager.
#
# These rules exist because a scratch key was, at one point during development,
# sitting in `cloud/phase-b-licensing/.keyscratch/private.pem` with nothing
# stopping it from being committed. `*.pem` is broad on purpose: a build that
# needs a legitimate public key in PEM form can `!`-negate it explicitly, and
# that deliberate exception is much cheaper than an accidental disclosure.
#
# See cloud/phase-b-licensing/docs/KEY-CEREMONY.md.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Issuer scratch space. `keygen --out .keyscratch` is the documented local
# workflow; the directory it writes must never reach a commit.
.keyscratch/
.keyscratch*/

# The patch manifest records absolute paths from the machine that ran the patch.
# Useful locally, meaningless (and mildly leaky) in a repo.
cloud/phase-b-licensing/patches/.applied-manifest.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working safety net.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `.snapshots/` holds pre-change copies taken before editing a file, so a change
# can be reverted byte-for-byte when there is no VCS to fall back on. It is a
# local convenience, not an artefact: never commit it.
.snapshots/

# Editor and manual-edit leftovers. A stale `.bak` of a live source file is how
# an edit gets applied to the wrong copy; these are never wanted in a commit.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.ts.bak

